1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,675
Every textbook says the same thing.

2
00:00:02,625 --> 00:00:06,670
Humans settled down, learned to farm, then built cities.

3
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:09,670
But this temple is 12,000 years old.

4
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:13,090
6,000 years before farming even existed.

5
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:16,465
Local shepherds always said the hilltop was sacred.

6
00:00:16,465 --> 00:00:19,431
Archaeologists ignored them for decades.

7
00:00:19,431 --> 00:00:22,999
In 1994, Klaus Schmidt started digging.

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,204
Massive carved pillars.

9
00:00:25,204 --> 00:00:27,352
Built by hunter-gatherers.

10
00:00:27,352 --> 00:00:29,988
20 times older than the pyramids.

11
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:33,056
And someone buried the whole thing on purpose.

12
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:36,386
They didn't build temples because they had civilization.

13
00:00:36,386 --> 00:00:39,624
They built civilization because they had temples.

